## Append propose-facts onto existing hypothetical facts
================================================================================

Context: Each Propose facts turn pushed agent patches onto the workbench
list with no merge, so a second prompt duplicated triples or left two
``set`` values on the same subject+predicate. Facts must accumulate in
append mode: keep prior facts, skip duplicates, and reconcile conflicts.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/simulation/Patch.py
   ``Patch.append_all`` drops exact duplicates, lets the latest ``set``
   win on a predicate, and cancels matching add/remove pairs.
2. src/api/routers/internal/simulation.py
   Return the merged patch list for ``/facts/agent`` and the SSE stream.
3. src/front/static/simulation/js/simulation-workbench.js
   Replace the workbench list with the merged payload instead of pushing.
4. src/agents/agent_simulation_facts/engine.py
   System prompt: append mode, skip EXISTING FACTS, replace conflicting sets.
5. src/agents/agent_simulation_facts/tools.py
   ``propose_patches`` schema documents append / replace behaviour.
6. tests/eval/datasets/agent_simulation_facts/regression.jsonl
   Ten append-mode examples with expected ``merged`` lists.
7. tests/eval/judges/simulation_facts.py
   Dry-run judge checks ``Patch.append_all`` against ``expected.merged``.
8. tests/units/simulation/test_simulation_core.py
   Cover duplicate, replace, cancel, and batch-dedup merge cases.
9. tests/units/simulation/test_simulation_runner_api.py
   Assert the propose-facts route returns the merged list.
10. tests/units/front/test_simulation_page_contract.py
    Require replace-not-push in ``proposeFacts``.
11. tests/units/agents/test_agent_simulation_facts.py
    Assert APPEND MODE in the system prompt; regression file ≥ 10 rows.
12. tests/eval/datasets/agent_simulation_facts/baseline.jsonl
    Add ``merged`` on skip-existing and enrich-desc-003.

